Package: svdpp
Title: SVD++ and Asymmetric-SVD Recommender Models
Version: 0.1.0
Authors@R:
    person("Akos", "Barta", email = "akos.barnabas.barta@wu.ac.at",
           role = c("aut", "cre", "cph"),
           comment = c(ORCID = "0009-0009-2933-3902"))
Description: Latent factor models for collaborative filtering from
    Koren (2008) <doi:10.1145/1401890.1401944>. SVD++ extends matrix
    factorisation in the style of the singular value decomposition (SVD)
    with implicit feedback; Asymmetric-SVD represents users only through
    the items they rated and can score new users without refitting; and the
    regularised baseline predictor models user and item biases. The models
    are written in R without compiled code. Each can be estimated by
    stochastic gradient descent, with the implicit-feedback updates grouped
    per user so that an epoch costs time linear in the number of ratings,
    or by full-batch optimisation with the limited-memory
    Broyden-Fletcher-Goldfarb-Shanno method with box constraints
    (L-BFGS-B), with gradients computed by sparse matrix algebra. Includes rating prediction, top-N
    recommendation, simulated data, and a helper to download the
    'MovieLens' data sets.
